What is Patchouli Oil?
Patchouli oil is an essential oil extracted from the leaves of Pogostemon cablin, a bushy herb native to tropical regions. Known for its distinctive earthy, musky aroma, it serves as a base note in over 65% of premium perfumes worldwide. Beyond perfumery, the oil's antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory properties make it valuable in pharmaceutical and wellness applications.
